.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt FSTAB 5
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm fstab
.Nd the file systems to mount
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pa /etc/fstab
lists file systems, one per line, for
.Xr mount 8
and
.Xr umount 8 ;
.Pa /etc/rc.d/mountcritlocal
mounts them at boot with
.Ql mount -a .
Blank lines and text after a
.Ql #
are ignored.
Each line has these fields, separated by blanks:
.Bl -enum
.It
.Em spec :
what to mount: the directory for
.Cm nullfs ,
or the file system's name, such as
.Dq tmpfs .
.It
.Em file :
the directory to mount it on.
.It
.Em vfstype :
.Cm oxfs
(the root),
.Cm tmpfs
or
.Cm nullfs ;
see
.Xr mount 8 .
.It
.Em mntops :
comma-separated options:
.Cm rw ,
and
.Cm noauto ,
which keeps
.Ql mount -a
from mounting it.
.It
.Em freq :
for
.Xr dump 8 ,
which doesn't exist yet; 0 if left out.
.It
.Em passno :
the order for checking file systems at boot, 0 for never; 0 if left out.
.El
.Pp
.Ql \e040
in a field stands for a space.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/fstab -compact
.It Pa /etc/fstab
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Device	Mountpoint	FStype	Options		Dump	Pass#
oxfs		/		oxfs	rw		1	1
tmpfs		/tmp		tmpfs	rw		0	0
/usr/src	/mnt/src	nullfs	rw,noauto	0	0
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr umount 8
.Sh HISTORY
An
.Nm
file appeared in
.Bx 4.0 .
